  "track": "paper",
  "title": "BaRISTA: Brain Scale Informed Spatiotemporal Representation of Human Intracranial Neural Activity",
  "status": "source_unresolved",
  "objective": "surpass_source_paper_same_task",
  "goal": "Surpass the source-paper result on the same task: Source program: sentence-onset and speech/non-speech classification under main random nonoverlap; four-task chronological classification including volume/optical flow; masked-channel waveform reconstruction; spatial encoding/masking, pretraining-seed, held-person-out and scaling analyses. One classification task or an invented pooled scalar cannot stand in for the complete registered scope.",
  "primary_outputs": [
    "Candidate method and outputs for the source task: Source program: sentence-onset and speech/non-speech classification under main random nonoverlap; four-task chronological classification including volume/optical flow; masked-channel waveform reconstruction; spatial encoding/masking, pretraining-seed, held-person-out and scaling analyses. One classification task or an invented pooled scalar cannot stand in for the complete registered scope.",
    "Source-paper comparison for Main random-nonoverlap sentence-onset ROC-AUC (numeric anchor only; complete original endpoint panel required): Classification ROC-AUC is the probability a positive score ranks above a negative, with half credit for ties, computed over all queries in a session/seed/fold. Native code uses roc_auc_score. Reconstruction reports MSE and R², but historical evaluation denominator/flattening and full reconstruction producer are not recovered; training token loss and locally declared MSE are different quantities."
  ],
  "success_criteria": [
    "Authenticate original recordings, channels, annotations, segmentation and all saved source splits; reconcile the person-6 paper/code session join.",
    "Exceed the source BaRISTA results on the identical original endpoint panel with matched pretraining people/movies, checkpoints, selection access and resources; report task-wise results against Table 1/2 and Table 16/17 separately.",
    "Retain all seven people, source seed/fold conditions and original encoding/masking comparisons. Neither a single successful subject nor an easier restricted model/subset is a whole-task win.",
    "Recover original reconstruction H/checkpoint and evaluation semantics before using Table 3 reconstruction claims; local MSE, token-training loss and original R² are not interchangeable. Complete the other retained full-paper conditions before claiming the registered program surpassed the paper.",
    "Meet frozen meaningful-effect and dependence-aware uncertainty rules. A new split, new across-task scalar or held-person-out result cannot be compared to the ordinary Table 1 baseline as if it were the same condition.",
    "The bound improvement contract must be improvement_ready and its complete same-task comparison and admission requirements must pass.",
    "Reproduction is calibration only; reconstructing a numerical result, changing the task or split, or achieving stronger significance alone is not success."
  ],
